<h3>Application 1 - Data Binding in Blazor</h3>

<!-- Two-Way Data Binding Section -->
<h4>Two-Way Data Binding</h4>

<label>Enter Your Name:</label>
<input type="text" @bind="userName" placeholder="Type your name here" />

<br />
<br />

<!-- One-Way Data Binding Section -->
<h4>One-Way Data Binding</h4>

<p>Greeting Message:</p>
<h5>Hello, @userName! Welcome to Blazor.</h5>

<hr />

<!-- Explanation Section -->
<h4>Explanation</h4>

<p>
    <b>Two-Way Data Binding:</b><br />
    The input field uses <code>@userName</code> to connect the textbox with the
    <code>userName</code> variable. Whenever the user types something,
    the variable updates automatically.
</p>

<p>
    <b>One-Way Data Binding:</b><br />
    The greeting message uses <code>@userName</code> to display data from
    the variable to the UI. It only shows the value and does not update
    the variable directly.
</p>

<p>
    <b>Difference:</b><br />
    One-way binding transfers data from the variable to the UI only,
    while two-way binding transfers data between the UI aend the variable
    in both directions.
</p>

@code {

    // Variable for storing user's name
    private string userName = "";

}